  "failure_resolution": "v0 exited 0xC0000409; v1 exception reporting exposed std::bad_alloc. This installed MSVC monotonic_buffer_resource::release() retains the cursor in a caller-supplied initial buffer when no upstream chunks exist. Reconstructing the PMR resource per batch fixed it. A separate bounded bump arena then removed PMR dispatch from the coroutine comparison.",
  "decision": "Do not enable coroutine registration: fixed-stack coroutine throughput is negative in all eight CPU conditions. Simple two-pass payload prefetch is positive in these constructed cases, but no full-model test or adoption of prefetch has been made.",
  "caveats": [
    "These are seven internal resource lookups, not expert slots, a GPU pipeline scheduler or a complete bbtree traversal port.",
    "The C++20 lanes yield once after std::map lookup, prefetching RecordingStorage.recording_index. std::map node traversal is synchronous.",
    "CPU-only measurements; no GPU speed/concurrency or full-model benefit claim.",
    "Some CPU controls drift by more than 20%; all rows, negative cases and failed prototypes are retained.",
    "No conclusion that coroutines are generally slower; bbtree uses different node layouts, per-node yields and a size cutoff.",
    "Fixed arena checks cover bounds, alignment, repeated reuse, resource order/deduplication, ownership and exception propagation."
  ],
